<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) HIKES GASOLINE PRICES.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) HIKES GASOLINE PRICES.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will raise gasoline prices by 4.7 drachmas per litre, effective on Thursday.</p>
<p>Transport diesel and heating oil prices will go up by 2.1 and 2.0 drachmas per litre respectively, DEP said.</p>
<p>The price adjustments came after higher world gasoline prices, up by $16.0 per metric tonne, higher transport diesel prices, up by $5.5 per metric tonne, higher heating oil prices, up by $5.2 per metric tonne, and a stronger dollar/drachma, up by 2.72 drachmas per dollar, it said.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
